{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.9ec41393c7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-629","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Kowalski is a Norwegian composer.</li><li>In 1974, Kowalski wrote <i>Small Season</i>, a symphony.</li><li><i>Small Season</i> draws on folk melodies from the composer's childhood village.</li><li><i>Small Season</i> has been performed by orchestras on four continents.</li><li>Kowalski trained as a concert pianist.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize the success of Small Season.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Small Season</i> was written in 1974.","Ingrid Kowalski trained as a concert pianist.","<i>Small Season</i>, a symphony by Kowalski, draws on folk melodies from the composer's childhood village.","<i>Small Season</i> has been performed by orchestras on four continents."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It reports what the work achieved. The other choices describe its features, its date, or the creator's background."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.cff75d6c92","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-634","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Varga is a Peruvian architect.</li><li>In 2020, Varga designed the Silver Lake Train Station.</li><li>The Silver Lake Train Station is lit almost entirely by skylights during the day.</li><li>The Silver Lake Train Station drew more than a million visitors in its first year.</li><li>Varga studied engineering before turning to architecture.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize the success of the Silver Lake Train Station.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Silver Lake Train Station, designed by Varga, is lit almost entirely by skylights during the day.","The Silver Lake Train Station drew more than a million visitors in its first year.","Kofi Varga studied engineering before turning to architecture.","The Silver Lake Train Station was designed in 2020."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It reports what the work achieved. The other choices describe its features, its date, or the creator's background."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.58041ee916","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-636","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Novak is a Nigerian choreographer.</li><li>In 1986, Novak created <i>Copper Orchard</i>, a ballet.</li><li><i>Copper Orchard</i> combines classical ballet with street dance.</li><li><i>Copper Orchard</i> won a major dance award.</li><li>Novak danced professionally for fifteen years.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize the success of Copper Orchard.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Copper Orchard</i> won a major dance award.","<i>Copper Orchard</i> was created in 1986.","<i>Copper Orchard</i>, a ballet by Novak, combines classical ballet with street dance.","Hana Novak danced professionally for fifteen years."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It reports what the work achieved. The other choices describe its features, its date, or the creator's background."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.f4a67b98a0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-638","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Takeda is an Australian novelist.</li><li>In 2016, Takeda published <i>Wild Shore</i>, a novel.</li><li><i>Wild Shore</i> alternates between the present day and the 1950s.</li><li><i>Wild Shore</i> spent a year on national bestseller lists.</li><li>Takeda studied history at university.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize when Wild Shore was completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Wild Shore</i>, a novel by Takeda, alternates between the present day and the 1950s.","<i>Wild Shore</i> spent a year on national bestseller lists.","Sofia Takeda is an Australian novelist.","<i>Wild Shore</i> was published in 2016."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It centers on the year the work was completed. The other choices describe a feature, an achievement, or the person, with no date."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.98aca33fbc","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-641","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Iyer is a Filipino choreographer.</li><li>In 2005, Iyer created <i>Wild Field</i>, a dance piece.</li><li><i>Wild Field</i> is performed without any music.</li><li><i>Wild Field</i> won a major dance award.</li><li>Iyer trained in both ballet and traditional dance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize when Wild Field was completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Wild Field</i> was created in 2005.","<i>Wild Field</i> won a major dance award.","Samuel Iyer is a Filipino choreographer.","<i>Wild Field</i>, a dance piece by Iyer, is performed without any music."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It centers on the year the work was completed. The other choices describe a feature, an achievement, or the person, with no date."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.19f8e46dcf","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-647","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Imani Petrov is a Ghanaian choreographer.</li><li>In 2017, Petrov created <i>Wild House</i>, a ballet.</li><li><i>Wild House</i> was inspired by the movements of migrating birds.</li><li><i>Wild House</i> won a major dance award.</li><li>Petrov trained in both ballet and traditional dance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize when Wild House was completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Imani Petrov is a Ghanaian choreographer.","<i>Wild House</i>, a ballet by Petrov, was inspired by the movements of migrating birds.","<i>Wild House</i> won a major dance award.","<i>Wild House</i> was created in 2017."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It centers on the year the work was completed. The other choices describe a feature, an achievement, or the person, with no date."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.48f660b5c2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-648","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Halvorsen is a Norwegian choreographer.</li><li>In 2017, Halvorsen created <i>Northern Light</i>, a dance piece.</li><li><i>Northern Light</i> is performed without any music.</li><li><i>Northern Light</i> won a major dance award.</li><li>Halvorsen trained in both ballet and traditional dance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize when Northern Light was completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Northern Light</i> was created in 2017.","Elias Halvorsen is a Norwegian choreographer.","<i>Northern Light</i> won a major dance award.","<i>Northern Light</i>, a dance piece by Halvorsen, is performed without any music."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It centers on the year the work was completed. The other choices describe a feature, an achievement, or the person, with no date."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.db21d40bd3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-2","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Rahman is a marine biologist.</li><li>Rahman wanted to find out whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.</li><li>Rahman recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.</li><li>Rahman found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.</li><li>Rahman concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Rahman found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.","To investigate the question, Rahman recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.","Marine biologist Jonas Rahman set out to learn whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.","Rahman concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.94c6d3f8e0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-43","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Halvorsen is a geologist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.</li><li>Halvorsen measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.</li><li>Halvorsen found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Geologist Amara Halvorsen set out to learn whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.","Halvorsen concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","Halvorsen found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.","To investigate the question, Halvorsen measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.f7d644e704","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-82","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Anika Brennan is a botanist.</li><li>Brennan wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Brennan grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Brennan found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Brennan concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Brennan found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","To investigate the question, Brennan grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Brennan concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","Botanist Anika Brennan set out to learn whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.c580cf8a26","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-98","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Mensah is an education researcher.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Mensah had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Mensah found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Mensah concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Education researcher Elias Mensah set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.","Mensah found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","To investigate the question, Mensah had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.f46a75bc51","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-100","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Sato is an education researcher.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Sato had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Sato found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Sato concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Education researcher Lucía Sato set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.","Sato found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","Sato concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","To investigate the question, Sato had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.a9c18cd561","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-129","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Novak is a public health researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Public health researcher Felipe Novak set out to learn whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.","To investigate the question, Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.","Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.5b9c4329d5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-144","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Castellano is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Castellano fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Castellano found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Castellano concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Castellano found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.","To investigate the question, Castellano fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Castellano concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","Marine ecologist Ravi Castellano set out to learn whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.15d9c5911f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-155","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Okafor is a climate scientist.</li><li>Okafor wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Okafor compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Okafor found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Okafor concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Climate scientist Ravi Okafor set out to learn whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.","Okafor found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","Okafor concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","To investigate the question, Okafor compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.17d74c0b41","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-164","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Kowalski is a veterinary scientist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.</li><li>Kowalski played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.</li><li>Kowalski found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Veterinary scientist Lucía Kowalski set out to learn whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.","Kowalski concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.","Kowalski found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.","To investigate the question, Kowalski played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.e4624a1e3b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-167","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Castellano is a veterinary scientist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.</li><li>Castellano played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.</li><li>Castellano found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.</li><li>Castellano concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Castellano concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.","Veterinary scientist Priya Castellano set out to learn whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.","To investigate the question, Castellano played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.","Castellano found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."}
